1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,200
The Americans stood on the Elbe, just 85 kilometres from Berlin.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:05,600
Then they stopped.

3
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:09,600
Eisenhower had written to Stalin that he would not push on to Berlin.

4
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:12,660
Stalin replied that Berlin no longer mattered.

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:14,720
At the same time, he ordered the attack.

6
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:21,660
On 16 April 1945, 2.5 million Soviet and Polish soldiers attacked.

7
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:25,900
Zhukov was to strike head-on across the Oder, Konev around from the south.

8
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:32,240
At the Seelow Heights, Zhukov switched on 143 searchlights to blind the defenders.

9
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:36,900
But they only lit up smoke and dust, and his tanks got stuck in the marshes.

10
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:38,540
Konev advanced faster.

11
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,340
By 25 April, Berlin was surrounded.

12
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:45,720
That same day, Americans and Soviets met at Torgau on the Elbe.

13
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:48,360
Inside the city, every street was fought over.

14
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:51,880
On 30 April, Soviet soldiers stormed the Reichstag.

15
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:54,760
That afternoon, Hitler killed himself in his bunker.

16
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:57,220
On 2 May, Berlin surrendered.

17
00:00:57,340 --> 00:01:06,940
The Red Army lost over 350,000 men killed and wounded, around 100,000 German soldiers died, along with tens of thousands of civilians.

18
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,620
The Soviet soldiers' inscriptions are still on the walls of the Reichstag today.
